course: dictionary
lesson: 243
title: Alone and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word alone can mean a few different things, so read the sentence to find which one fits. Most often it means without anyone else: «Bullies pick on children who are alone more often» means children with nobody around them.
explain: Alone can also mean without help, or only, just that one. «You alone know the secret» means you are the only person who knows it. To check, put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
explain: Leave alone is a phrase, and its words do not add up to its meaning. «Leave the bird alone» means do not touch or bother it. When a phrase puzzles you, learn it as one unit.
fact: Alone means without anyone else: if you are alone, nobody is with you.
fact: Alone can also mean without help, as in doing a job on your own.
fact: «You alone know the secret» means only you, nobody else.
fact: «Leave alone» means do not touch or bother, and «all alone» and «on your own» are other phrases with the same kind of meaning.
fact: Alone can be an adjective, as in «The dog was alone», or an adverb, as in «You alone know».
exercise: Sam will put up the tent without any help. Which phrase means this? | Leave alone | Once upon a time | Out of breath | *On your own
exercise: «You alone know the secret.» What does alone mean here? | Left in peace | *Only you, and nobody else | Without anyone else with you | Lonely and sad
exercise: The sign says «Leave the bird alone.» What should you do? | *Do not touch or bother it | Chase it across the park | Take it home with you | Feed it some bread
test: «Gran was alone in the garden, reading.» What does alone mean here? | Without any help from anyone | *By herself, with nobody else there | Only in the mornings | With her dog for company
test: Which phrase means do not touch or bother? | *Leave alone | Tidy up | All alone | Shout loudly
exam: How can you check you have chosen the right meaning of alone? | Ask a friend to guess for you | Count the letters in the word | *Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the first word of the sentence
